<title>TUNISIA: Tunisia lifts airport tax to attract tourists.</title>
<headline>Tunisia lifts airport tax to attract tourists.</headline>
<dateline>TUNIS 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tunisia has decided to lift airliner taxes at two international airports for the next three years to encourage tourist flights, officials said on Friday.</p>
<p>The airports are at Tabarka in the northwestern region and Tozeur, in the southeast. Both are in tourist areas for which direct links with Europe were encouraged, they said.</p>
<p>President Zine al-Abidine Ben Ali took the decision after a meeting with Transport Minister Sadok Rabeh and Tahar Haj Ali, chairman of the national airliner Tunis Air.</p>
<p>Ben Ali was also informed about the recent installation in Tunis-Carthage airport of a new up-to-date radar system, they added.</p>
